  "reasoning": "The patient presents with pain localized to the neck, arms, and legs, alongside difficulty maintaining balance and feelings of dizziness ('woozy'). These symptoms suggest compression or irritation of nerves and potentially the spinal cord in the cervical region. The combination of neck pain radiating into the upper and lower extremities, coupled with balance disturbances and lightheadedness, is a classic clinical presentation of degenerative changes in the cervical spine. Based on symptom matching and clinical correlation, this points directly to cervical spondylosis.",
